    "text": "Done! I've implemented a bounded stack in Cuis with the following:\n\n**BoundedStack class** (`BoundedStack` category):\n- `capacity:` class method \u2014 creates a stack with validation that capacity must be a positive integer\n- `initialize:` \u2014 sets up the internal array and indices\n- `push:` \u2014 adds an object; fails if stack is full\n- `pop` \u2014 removes and returns the top object; fails if stack is empty\n- `top` \u2014 returns the top without removing; fails if stack is empty\n- `isEmpty` and `size` \u2014 query methods\n\n**Comprehensive tests** (`BoundedStack-Tests` category):\n- Creating with valid/invalid capacities\n- Push and pop operations with size tracking\n- Top operation preserves stack state\n- Error handling for full stack, empty pop, and empty top\n- Error message validation\n\nAll 8 tests pass. The image is saved and ready to review."
